==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*15 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] spawns as the boss after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
High level Cats are recommended. It is possible to clear this stage normally even with lower levels (30-40). When doing this, you should either kill or severely cripple Rangmaster before THE FOLIVOREAN spawns since he will destroy your ranged attackers and give Rangmaster an unobstructed path to your base. Higher levels make this stage a cakewalk. Strong units with range higher than 350 (i.e. [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs]] or [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|dragons]]) are vitally important to killing Rangmaster quickly.

==='''Strategy 1 (Cheese / Rush)'''===
{{Lineup
|Li'l Macho Cat
|Catasaurus
|Necro-Dancer Cat
|Skelecat
|Hyper Mr.
|Manic Mohawk Cat|30
|Manic Eraser Cat|30
|Can Can Cat|40
|talent8 = Move Speed Up Lv. 10, Extra Money
|Courier Cat|35
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|30
|notes = [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] is recommended.
}}

When the stage begins, save up for Can Can and immediately start spamming everything but Bahamut. If the can can hits the Snache instead of Doge Dark, restart the stage (the 10 second rule most likely has not passed). If it does, the doge will give you enough money to last you a good chunk of the stage. Now, loosen up on the meat shield spam and save for Bahamut. When you hit the base, Ragin' Gory will spawn around that timeframe, but will get absolutely melted by the courier stack you have. Lophiiformes Angaburu will spawn too late to do anything, as you will be dishing out enough combined DPS from can can, courier and bahamut to destroy the base before Lophiiformes Angaburu can do anything.

This strategy is pretty consistent, but if you have Bahamut's [[Explosion]] Talent, the chances of winning is effectively guaranteed, as Bahamut's piercing attacks are powerful enough to protect him from the Ragin' Gory even without meatshields.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]]: A great rusher that can eliminate Ragin' Gory with ease. Beware of their high cost, however, and only use them to take out the initial Ragin' Gory, not the Doge Darks that follow it.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: Despite having incredibly frail health, Cat Researcher is able to score consistent shield pierces on Rangmaster, heavily lowering their effective health and giving easy opportunities for your other units to hit for big damage. If you choose to use them, make sure to protect them well.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Phenomenal form of chip damage on both Lophiiformes Angaburu and Rangmaster, though she can usually only score a single hit on Rangmaster before falling. Unlocking her savage blow also allows her to more consistently zombie-kill Angaburu, which can help greatly in lessening this stage's difficulty.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]]: An absolute menace for every Aku enemy anywhere, he can pierce Rangmasters shield and knocks him back in 2-3 hits at lvl 40. He can also survive a hit from THE FOLIVOREAN and deliver a good chunk of damage quickly.
*[[Kaguya of the Coast (Uber Rare Cat)|The Southern Sunflare]]: With proper meatshielding this unit can outrange Rangmaster's [[Omni Strike]]s and Halt his progress pretty reliably. The peons don't push that hard in this stage so it is not unrealistic to have two Sunflares on the field at the same time.
*[[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Lionheart]]: At a high enough level, this unit OHKOs both Angaburus if it ever manages to get a hit on them. While it doesn't help with the main threat of the stage as much, getting rid of the annoying slowing [[Mini-Surge]]s can really tip the scales in your favor when fighting Rangmaster.
*[[Shadow (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow]]: Being a surprisingly good fit for this stage, Shadow's mix of high speed and very long range help in outranging most threats and especially destroying Angaburu and Ragin' Gory. His usage against THE FOLIVOREAN is poor though, requiring more support.

